WEBVTT

00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:04.917
When you read a recursive query, identify the anchor term first.

00:00:04.917 --> 00:00:08.097
Ask which rows start the process.

00:00:08.097 --> 00:00:10.802
Then identify the recursive term.

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:14.402
Ask how the current level connects to the next level.

00:00:14.402 --> 00:00:20.167
For an employee hierarchy, the connection is usually the manager relationship.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:26.077
A manager I D in one row points to an employee I D in another row.

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:30.687
Adding a depth value can show how far we are from the starting point.

00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:34.482
A path value can show the route through the hierarchy.

00:00:34.482 --> 00:00:38.740
These extra fields make recursion much easier to inspect.
